{
 "comment": "loans_interest s.194A coverage at the reference's current head, a firm (a deductor): interest booked net of a TDS-payable ledger, counted gross, then a TDS catch-up journal, covering the rate (Covered Loan: no s.194A finding, a TDS-seen finding); TDS short of the rate (Partly Loan: partly covered); TDS dated before any interest covers none of it (Early TDS Loan); a LIC and a financial-corporation lender, which the current rules exempt, over the threshold with no TDS (no finding); two interest ledgers on one loan, one of them also classified TDS payable, which never makes it a TDS line (Multi Loan); interest whose s.194A rate ends in half a paisa, TDS on a separate voucher the same day and a TDS reversal, covered only within the tolerance (Round Loan); one TDS journal debiting two loans, counted for neither, which LOAN-1 names for both (Twin A, Twin B).",
